{%- comment -%}
  ElmsNest v2 PDP — §4.7 "עוד לא בטוחים? לא חייבים."  ·  #env2-pdp-ask  ·  spine answers #7 + #8.

  Two jobs, one screen: the specialist line (why here and not a marketplace) and the two ways to
  NOT buy yet — send a photo of the place, or start from the smallest thing the product sells.
  No comparison table, no competitor, no claim (BRIEF §11 / do-not §6.3): the "why here" is a
  quotation from the store's own «מי אנחנו» page and three facts the page has already kept above.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ what is authored, what is derived
  Authored brand copy (settings, editable): the eyebrow, the two heading lines, the lead sentences,
  the quote and its citation. NOTHING here is a product claim.
  Derived from the product, never typed:
    · the small step's own words — the cheapest AVAILABLE row of elmsnest-v2-pdp-variants, printed as
      its option value + its price ("להתחיל מ־5 מטר — 89.90 ₪" · "להתחיל מיחידה אחת — 169.90 ₪" ·
      "להתחיל מ־6W — 219.90 ₪"). The row index it selects is the ledger row it names.
    · the lead's last clause, which follows the same unit: אורך (מ׳) / יחידה (single or a count) /
      עוצמה (W) / a neutral phrase for anything else, and nothing at all when there is no ledger.
    · the lead's FIRST sentence, which follows §3.7's three-state honesty rule (below).

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ the §4.2 agreement (§3.7, §8.2)
  §4.7's lead opens "אמרנו למעלה מתי היא לא מתאימה" — true only when §4.2 actually printed a negative.
  custom.not_fit_for is EMPTY on all 27 products today, so §4.2 renders its "how to choose" mode and
  this section must say the same thing. The test here is byte-identical to elmsnest-v2-pdp-fit's:
  the metafield must match one of the FOUR approved negatives exactly and, when the metafield is
  blank, the place's own approved pair stands in — gated on solar for the three negatives that are
  only true on a battery, exactly as §4.2 gates them (BRIEF §4 row 2 names the pair and the
  description as the honest sources). When neither yields a negative — product C — the first
  sentence becomes "אמרנו למעלה איך בוחרים נכון." — the same words §4.2 uses in that state. lead_mode lets an
  integrator pin it if §4.2 was overridden from its own section settings (which this file cannot read).
  This section says nothing about power, ever, on any product — so §3.7 cannot be breached here.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ the closing photograph (CREATIVE-10)
  Below the ledger the page stopped producing photographic events: the third and fourth quarters of
  every PDP measured 2.6–9.3 % lit against the homepage's 16.7 %, i.e. grey text on black for the
  last 4,000 px. This section now closes the page on the thing it opens with — the product's own
  light, full bleed, with the §3.1 veil carrying the copy exactly as the stage carries it. One
  enormous thing on the last screen (§3.3 / §8). It is a section setting, so it can be switched off,
  and the photograph is resolved through elmsnest-v2-pdp-image's own "ask" slot (§3.5) — never a
  baked-text slide, and deliberately never the hero's own frame, so the page does not open and close
  on the same picture.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ the two calls to action
  1. The small step (primary, filled pill). An <a href="#env2-pdp-ledger"> so it works with no JS at
     all; with JS it clicks that row's own button inside §4.4 (which drives the stage price, string
     and sticky bar through the one code path that already exists) and scrolls back to the stage.
     §8.3: a filled .env2-btn ANCHOR loses its ink to .env2-section a{color:inherit} (0,1,1) and
     renders 1.21:1 — so the colour is set from .env2-pdp-ask a.env2-pdp-ask__start (0,2,1), and the
     computed colour was checked in the render, not assumed.
  2. The photo check (ghost). Rendered by snippets/elmsnest-v2-pdp-photo-cta — the ONE place the
     mailto / wa.me branch lives. settings.whatsapp_number is empty, so it is a mailto and no label
     can claim a WhatsApp channel; this file builds no URL of its own and names no channel.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ motion (§3.3)
  Exactly one thing switches on, and it is not text (do-not §6.19 forbids a text fade-in): the
  hairline that carries the quote lights from .3 to full when the quote arrives, and the closing
  photograph lights with it. Every word is server-rendered at full opacity in every state.
  Reduced motion / no JS: both are lit.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ no JS
  The section is complete and buyable without JavaScript: both CTAs are ordinary anchors, the small
  step scrolls to the ledger where every row carries its own POST form, the lamp is lit, and the
  quote, the lead and the citation are plain server-rendered text.

  Plumbing: elmsnest-v2-core (rendered from layout/theme.liquid on every page) supplies the tokens,
  the fonts, the .env2-* helpers, [data-lamp] and window.env2. This section renders no global, no
  ground and no font link (§8.2).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign env2_RS = '~~R~~'
  assign env2_FS = '~~F~~'
-%}
{%- capture env2_model -%}{%- if product -%}{%- render 'elmsnest-v2-pdp-variants', product: product -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- liquid
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- the ledger model (CONTRACT-PDP §3)
  # It prints RAW TEXT, so the call above is captured. A blank product prints nothing at all, and
  # every branch below degrades to "no small step" rather than to an empty or invented one.
  assign env2_recs = env2_model | strip | split: env2_RS
  assign env2_m = env2_recs[0] | split: env2_FS
  assign env2_has = false
  if env2_m[0] == 'meta' and env2_recs.size > 1
    assign env2_has = true
  endif
  assign env2_mode = env2_m[1] | default: 'variants'

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- the small step: the cheapest row
  # Rows come in the option's own value order, which is not always the cheapest first, and a sold-out
  # row is not somewhere to start — so an available row always wins, and price decides among them.
  assign env2_si = 0
  assign env2_sprice = ''
  assign env2_sn = ''
  assign env2_su = ''
  assign env2_skey = ''
  assign env2_best = 0
  assign env2_found = false
  assign env2_afound = false
  if env2_has
    for env2_rec in env2_recs offset: 1
      assign r = env2_rec | split: env2_FS
      assign rc = r[11] | plus: 0
      assign take = false
      if r[14] == '1'
        if env2_afound == false or rc < env2_best
          assign take = true
          assign env2_afound = true
        endif
      elsif env2_afound == false
        if env2_found == false or rc < env2_best
          assign take = true
        endif
      endif
      if take
        assign env2_found = true
        assign env2_best = rc
        assign env2_si = r[1] | plus: 0
        assign env2_sprice = r[10]
        assign env2_sn = r[6]
        assign env2_su = r[7]
        assign env2_skey = r[3]
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  # The step's WORDS are the row's own option value — its first segment, so "5 מ׳ / 20 נורות"
  # becomes "5 מ׳" and "6W" stays "6W" — with one typographic expansion, the unit מ׳ written out as
  # מטר, which is how §4.7 prints it. Nothing is composed out of parts, so a value this build has
  # never seen ("1.5×1.5 מ׳ / 96 LED", "1 'יח", "אור חם 3000K") still names itself correctly.
  assign env2_seg = env2_skey | split: ' / ' | first | default: '' | strip
  assign env2_seg = env2_seg | replace: 'מ׳', 'מטר'

  # which last clause the lead gets — decided by the row's OWN parsed unit, never by a typed guess
  assign env2_len = '~מ׳~מטר~מטרים~'
  assign env2_cnt = '~יח׳~יח~יחידה~יחידות~'
  assign env2_cnt2 = "~'יח~"
  assign env2_probe = '~' | append: env2_su | append: '~'
  assign env2_kind = 'plain'
  if env2_mode == 'single'
    assign env2_kind = 'single'
  elsif env2_sn == blank or env2_seg == blank
    assign env2_kind = 'plain'
  elsif env2_len contains env2_probe
    assign env2_kind = 'length'
  elsif env2_cnt contains env2_probe or env2_cnt2 contains env2_probe
    assign env2_kind = 'count'
  elsif env2_su == 'W'
    assign env2_kind = 'power'
  else
    assign env2_kind = 'other'
  endif

  assign env2_show_step = false
  if section.settings.show_start_small and env2_has and env2_sprice != blank
    assign env2_show_step = true
  endif

  # the step's destination: the ledger row by default, or a URL the merchant pinned
  assign env2_step_href = '#env2-pdp-ledger'
  assign env2_by_row = true
  if section.settings.start_small_target == 'url'
    assign env2_by_row = false
    assign env2_step_href = section.settings.start_small_url | default: '' | strip
    if env2_step_href == ''
      assign env2_step_href = product.url | default: '#env2-pdp-ledger'
    endif
  endif

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- did §4.2 print a negative? (§3.7)
  assign env2_ok_neg = '~המקום כמעט אינו מקבל אור יום~נדרש אור חזק וקבוע לאורך כל הלילה~צריך אור חזק — זו אינה מטרתה~נדרשת התקנה מיוחדת או חיבור קבוע~'
  assign env2_solar_clause = 'המקום כמעט אינו מקבל אור יום'
  assign env2_pwr = product.metafields.custom.power_source | default: '' | strip
  assign env2_solar = false
  if env2_pwr == 'סולארי'
    assign env2_solar = true
  elsif env2_pwr == ''
    assign env2_hay = product.description | strip_html | append: ' ' | append: product.title
    if env2_hay contains 'סולארי'
      assign env2_solar = true
    endif
  endif
  assign env2_neg = product.metafields.custom.not_fit_for | default: '' | strip
  if env2_neg != ''
    assign env2_probe2 = '~' | append: env2_neg | append: '~'
    unless env2_ok_neg contains env2_probe2
      assign env2_neg = ''
    endunless
  endif
  if env2_neg == env2_solar_clause and env2_solar == false
    assign env2_neg = ''
  endif
  # the same fallback §4.2 now uses, so the two sections cannot disagree about what the page said:
  # the place's OWN approved pair when the metafield is blank, and only where it is literally true.
  if env2_neg == ''
    assign env2_ptype = product.type | default: ''
    if env2_ptype == 'גרילנדות ותאורה דקורטיבית'
      assign env2_neg = 'צריך אור חזק — זו אינה מטרתה'
    elsif env2_solar and env2_ptype == 'תאורת שביל, עמוד וגינה'
      assign env2_neg = 'המקום כמעט אינו מקבל אור יום'
    elsif env2_solar and env2_ptype == 'תאורת קיר'
      assign env2_neg = 'נדרש אור חזק וקבוע לאורך כל הלילה'
    elsif env2_solar and env2_ptype == 'ספוטים, פרוז׳קטורים ותאורה ניידת'
      assign env2_neg = 'נדרשת התקנה מיוחדת או חיבור קבוע'
    endif
  endif
  assign env2_has_neg = false
  if env2_neg != ''
    assign env2_has_neg = true
  endif
  if section.settings.lead_mode == 'notfit'
    assign env2_has_neg = true
  elsif section.settings.lead_mode == 'choose'
    assign env2_has_neg = false
  endif

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- the lead, assembled
  assign env2_lead = section.settings.lead_choose | default: '' | strip
  if env2_has_neg
    assign env2_lead = section.settings.lead | default: '' | strip
  endif
  assign env2_step_txt = section.settings.lead_step | default: '' | strip
  if env2_step_txt != ''
    if env2_show_step
      if env2_kind == 'length'
        assign env2_step_txt = env2_step_txt | append: ', או להתחיל מהאורך הקצר.'
      elsif env2_kind == 'single'
        assign env2_step_txt = env2_step_txt | append: ', או להתחיל מיחידה אחת.'
      elsif env2_kind == 'count'
        # never "מיחידה אחת" here: on a set product the smallest row is 2 or 4 units, not one
        assign env2_step_txt = env2_step_txt | append: ', או להתחיל מהכמות הקטנה.'
      elsif env2_kind == 'power'
        assign env2_step_txt = env2_step_txt | append: ', או להתחיל מהעוצמה הנמוכה.'
      else
        # an axis this build cannot characterise (a colour temperature, a model name): the button
        # below says exactly what it starts from, so the sentence does not invent an adjective
        assign env2_step_txt = env2_step_txt | append: '.'
      endif
    else
      assign env2_step_txt = env2_step_txt | append: '.'
    endif
    if env2_lead == ''
      assign env2_lead = env2_step_txt
    else
      assign env2_lead = env2_lead | append: ' ' | append: env2_step_txt
    endif
  endif

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- the quote(s)
  assign env2_quotes = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'quote'
-%}
{%- assign env2_photo = blank -%}
{%- if section.settings.show_photo and product != blank -%}
  {%- capture env2_pi -%}{%- render 'elmsnest-v2-pdp-image', product: product, slot: 'ask', index: section.settings.photo_index -%}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign env2_pi = env2_pi | plus: 0 -%}
  {%- assign env2_photo = section.settings.photo_image | default: product.images[env2_pi] | default: product.featured_image -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%} the step's label: the row's own value + the row's own price, or the merchant's own line {%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture env2_step_label -%}
  {%- if section.settings.start_small_label != blank -%}
    {{- section.settings.start_small_label -}}
  {%- elsif env2_kind == 'single' -%}
    להתחיל מיחידה אחת — <bdi>{{ env2_sprice }}</bdi>&nbsp;&#8362;
  {%- elsif env2_kind == 'plain' -%}
    להתחיל מ־<bdi>{{ env2_sprice }}</bdi>&nbsp;&#8362;
  {%- else -%}
    להתחיל מ־<bdi>{{ env2_seg }}</bdi> — <bdi>{{ env2_sprice }}</bdi>&nbsp;&#8362;
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
<section id="env2-pdp-ask" data-env2-pdp-ask class="env2-section env2-pdp-ask{% if env2_photo != blank %} env2-pdp-ask--photo{% endif %}" dir="rtl" style="scroll-margin-top:90px;--env2-stars:{% if env2_photo != blank %}.2{% else %}.62{% endif %}" aria-labelledby="env2-pdp-ask-h2">
  <div class="env2-stars" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  {%- if env2_photo != blank -%}
    <div class="env2-pdp-ask__bg" data-lamp aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="env2-ph env2-pdp-ask__ph">
        {{ env2_photo | image_url: width: 1800 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', decoding: 'async', widths: '600,900,1400,1800', sizes: '100vw', alt: '', class: 'env2-pdp-ask__img' }}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="env2-pdp-ask__veil" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="env2-wrap env2-pdp-ask__wrap">
    <div class="env2-pdp-ask__main">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="env2-eyebrow env2-pdp-ask__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.heading_line1 != blank or section.settings.heading_line2 != blank -%}
        <h2 id="env2-pdp-ask-h2" class="env2-h env2-pdp-ask__h2">
          {%- if section.settings.heading_line1 != blank -%}{{ section.settings.heading_line1 }}{%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.heading_line2 != blank -%}
            {%- if section.settings.heading_line1 != blank -%}<br>{%- endif -%}
            <span class="env2-glow env2-pdp-ask__glow">{{ section.settings.heading_line2 }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </h2>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if env2_lead != '' -%}
        <p class="env2-lead env2-pdp-ask__lead">{{ env2_lead }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="env2-pdp-ask__cta">
        {%- if env2_show_step -%}
          <a class="env2-btn env2-pdp-ask__start" href="{{ env2_step_href }}"
             {% if env2_by_row %}data-env2-ask-start data-i="{{ env2_si }}"{% endif %}>{{ env2_step_label | strip }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- render 'elmsnest-v2-pdp-photo-cta', product: product, style: 'ghost',
                   label: section.settings.photo_cta_label, subject: section.settings.mailto_subject,
                   body: section.settings.mailto_body, class: 'env2-pdp-ask__photo' -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- if env2_quotes.size > 0 -%}
      <div class="env2-pdp-ask__side">
        {%- for block in env2_quotes -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign qtext = block.settings.text | default: '' | strip
            assign qfirst = qtext | slice: 0, 1
            unless qfirst == '«'
              assign qtext = '«' | append: qtext | append: '»'
            endunless
          -%}
          {%- if qtext != '«»' -%}
            <figure class="env2-pdp-ask__quote" data-lamp {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              <blockquote class="env2-pdp-ask__q">{{ qtext }}</blockquote>
              {%- if block.settings.cite != blank or block.settings.link_label != blank -%}
                <figcaption class="env2-pdp-ask__cite">
                  {%- if block.settings.cite != blank -%}<span class="env2-pdp-ask__from">{{ block.settings.cite }}</span>{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if block.settings.link_label != blank and block.settings.link_url != blank -%}
                    <a class="env2-link env2-pdp-ask__a" href="{{ block.settings.link_url }}">{{ block.settings.link_label }} <span aria-hidden="true">&#8592;</span></a>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </figcaption>
              {%- endif -%}
            </figure>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
/* ---------- §4.7 PDP ask: the specialist line + the small step ----------
   Composition nobody else on this page uses (do-not §6.20): a two-column split whose halves are
   aligned on their BOTTOM edge — the heading, the lead and the two buttons at the start side, the
   quotation alone at the end side. No surface, no box, no card; the only ground is the closing
   photograph and the §3.1 veil over it. */
.env2-pdp-ask{padding-block:100px}
/* the closing photograph: full bleed behind the section, the copy carried on the §3.1 veil exactly as
   the stage carries it. The head sits low so the top of the band is photograph, not type. */
.env2-pdp-ask--photo{position:relative;isolation:isolate;overflow:clip;padding-block:clamp(150px,20vw,260px) clamp(84px,9vw,110px)}
.env2-pdp-ask__bg{position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:-2}
.env2-pdp-ask__bg[data-lamp] .env2-pdp-ask__ph{position:absolute;inset:0;background:#05070c;border-radius:0}
.env2-pdp-ask__bg[data-lamp] .env2-pdp-ask__ph img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:50% 42%;filter:brightness(calc(.1 + .34*var(--lit,1))) saturate(.85);transition:filter 1.6s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1);transform:none}
.env2-pdp-ask__bg[data-lamp] .env2-pdp-ask__ph::after{display:none}
.env2-pdp-ask__veil{position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:-1;pointer-events:none;background:radial-gradient(74% 58% at 100% 76%,rgba(4,7,14,.62),rgba(4,7,14,0) 76%),linear-gradient(0deg,var(--env2-sky-2) 0,rgba(15,26,47,.94) 16%,rgba(15,26,47,.82) 38%,rgba(15,26,47,.5) 66%,rgba(15,26,47,.2) 88%),linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(2,3,6,.5),rgba(2,3,6,0) 34%)}
.env2-pdp-ask--photo .env2-pdp-ask__h2.env2-h{text-shadow:0 2px 40px rgba(0,0,0,.55)}
.env2-pdp-ask--photo .env2-pdp-ask__lead.env2-lead,
.env2-pdp-ask--photo .env2-pdp-ask__q,
.env2-pdp-ask--photo .env2-pdp-ask__cite{text-shadow:0 1px 14px rgba(0,0,0,.6)}
.env2-pdp-ask__wrap{position:relative;z-index:1;display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.1fr) minmax(0,.9fr);align-items:end;gap:clamp(30px,6vw,100px)}
.env2-pdp-ask__main{min-inline-size:0}

.env2-pdp-ask__eyebrow{margin-block-end:24px}
.env2-pdp-ask__h2.env2-h{font-size:clamp(34px,4.9vw,72px);max-inline-size:14ch}
.env2-pdp-ask__glow{display:block}
.env2-pdp-ask__lead.env2-lead{margin-block-start:22px;font-size:clamp(16px,1.4vw,20px);line-height:1.55;max-inline-size:42ch}

/* the two ways to not-buy-yet, side by side: the small step first, the photo check beside it */
.env2-pdp-ask__cta{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:14px 18px;margin-block-start:38px}
/* §8.3: .env2-section a{color:inherit} is (0,1,1) and beats .env2-btn{color:…} (0,1,0) — an anchor
   styled as the filled pill would render ink-on-glow at 1.21:1. This selector is (0,2,1), so the
   button ink wins in every state. Measured in the render: #1a1206 on #ffd394 = 13.4:1. */
.env2-pdp-ask a.env2-pdp-ask__start,
.env2-pdp-ask a.env2-pdp-ask__start:hover,
.env2-pdp-ask a.env2-pdp-ask__start:focus-visible{color:var(--env2-btn-ink)}
/* border-box and white-space:normal are not decoration: .env2-btn is nowrap, the label is built from
   the product's own option value, and a long one ("1.5×1.5 מטר", "אור חם 3000K") would otherwise push
   a full-width mobile button past the viewport. The numbers stay unbreakable inside their own <bdi>. */
.env2-pdp-ask__start,.env2-pdp-ask__photo{box-sizing:border-box;white-space:normal}
/* §4.1's 52px and §6.18's 44px floor: .env2-btn{min-height:0} is (0,1,0) and sits later in the
   cascade (the layout's inline <style>), so the floor has to be stated at (0,2,x) — QA-03. */
.env2-pdp-ask a.env2-pdp-ask__start,.env2-pdp-ask .env2-pdp-ask__photo{min-block-size:52px}
.env2-pdp-ask__start{padding-inline:26px;text-align:center}
.env2-pdp-ask__start bdi{unicode-bidi:isolate;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap}

/* the quotation: FRL 400 on a hairline that is the one thing in this section that switches on.
   The words themselves never change opacity — a text fade-in is forbidden (do-not §6.19). */
.env2-pdp-ask__side{display:grid;gap:34px;min-inline-size:0}
.env2-pdp-ask__quote{position:relative;margin:0;padding-inline-start:28px}
.env2-pdp-ask__quote::before{content:"";position:absolute;inset-block:3px 3px;inset-inline-start:0;inline-size:1px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(233,185,110,.8),rgba(244,238,227,.1));opacity:calc(.3 + .7*var(--lit,1));transition:opacity 1.4s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1)}
.env2-pdp-ask__q{margin:0;font-family:var(--env2-serif);font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(22px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:-.005em;color:var(--env2-ink);text-wrap:balance}
.env2-pdp-ask__cite{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:6px 16px;margin-block-start:18px;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:300;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--env2-mute)}
.env2-pdp-ask__a{font-size:14px}

/* ---------- mobile: one column, the quote last, both buttons full width ---------- */
@media (max-width:900px){
  .env2-pdp-ask{padding-block:72px 64px}
  .env2-pdp-ask__wrap{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:44px}
  .env2-pdp-ask__eyebrow{margin-block-end:16px}
  .env2-pdp-ask__h2.env2-h{max-inline-size:none}
  .env2-pdp-ask__lead.env2-lead{margin-block-start:18px;max-inline-size:none}
  .env2-pdp-ask__cta{flex-direction:column;align-items:stretch;gap:12px;margin-block-start:30px}
  .env2-pdp-ask__start,.env2-pdp-ask__photo{inline-size:100%}
  .env2-pdp-ask--photo{padding-block:clamp(120px,34vw,180px) 64px}
  .env2-pdp-ask__side{gap:28px}
  .env2-pdp-ask__quote{padding-inline-start:20px}
  .env2-pdp-ask__cite{margin-block-start:14px}
  .env2-pdp-ask__a{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-block-size:44px}
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% javascript %}
/* §4.7's one behaviour: the small step selects the ledger row it names and takes the buyer back to
   the stage, so "start from the short one" is one tap rather than a scroll and a re-decision.
   Everything else in this section is server-rendered; with JS off the same anchor still scrolls to
   #env2-pdp-ledger, where that row carries its own POST form (§4.4), and the lamp is lit.
   The ledger owns variant state: clicking its row button drives the stage price, the drawn string
   and the sticky bar through the single code path that already exists — this file duplicates none
   of it. Ends with the CONTRACT's env2.observe fallback line. */
(function () {
  function init(el) {
    if (el.__env2PdpAsk) { return; }
    el.__env2PdpAsk = true;

    var step = el.querySelector('[data-env2-ask-start]');
    if (step) {
      step.addEventListener('click', function (ev) {
        var ledger = document.querySelector('[data-env2-pdp-ledger]');
        var row = null;
        if (ledger) {
          var want = step.getAttribute('data-i') || '0';
          var rows = ledger.querySelectorAll('[data-env2-pdp-ledger-row]');
          for (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {
            if (String(rows[i].getAttribute('data-i')) === String(want)) { row = rows[i]; }
          }
        }
        var pick = row ? row.querySelector('[data-env2-pdp-ledger-pick]') : null;
        var stage = document.getElementById('env2-pdp-stage');
        var target = stage || ledger;
        /* no ledger row and no stage on this page: let the browser follow the anchor as written */
        if (!pick && !target) { return; }
        /* the core also listens for a[href^="#env2-"] on the document and would scroll to the
           LEDGER, which is not where this button goes — so the click stops at this element. */
        if (ev.preventDefault) { ev.preventDefault(); }
        if (ev.stopPropagation) { ev.stopPropagation(); }
        if (pick) { pick.click(); }
        if (target && target.scrollIntoView) {
          var rm = (window.env2 && window.env2.rm) ||
            (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches);
          try {
            target.scrollIntoView({ behavior: rm ? 'auto' : 'smooth', block: 'start' });
          } catch (e) { target.scrollIntoView(); }
        }
      });
    }

    window.env2 ? env2.observe(el) : el.querySelectorAll('[data-lamp]').forEach(function (l) { l.classList.add('lit'); });
  }
  function boot(root) {
    var scope = (root && root.querySelectorAll) ? root : document;
    scope.querySelectorAll('[data-env2-pdp-ask]').forEach(init);
    if (scope !== document && scope.matches && scope.matches('[data-env2-pdp-ask]')) { init(scope); }
  }
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () { boot(document); });
  } else {
    boot(document);
  }
  document.addEventListener('shopify:section:load', function (e) { boot(e.target || document); });
})();
{% endjavascript %}

